  "lineage": "Song tradition of the Luo of the Lake Victoria region of western Kenya, around Siaya and Kisumu, in which a male singer accompanies himself on the eight-string nyatiti bowl lyre, marking the beat with an iron ring on his toe struck against the instrument and with ankle bells. Its repertoire includes praise songs and songs for funerals, and its interlocking lyre patterns shaped the guitar style of benga.",
